286
00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:21.056
Or is it a last will?

287
00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:26.636
Open the door.

288
00:24:42.010 --> 00:24:42.910
Park Geon-yeop?

289
00:24:43.396 --> 00:24:45.180
Huh, what's going on?

290
00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:47.383
F***, let go, you bastard.

291
00:24:50.383 --> 00:24:51.336
Get in the car.

292
00:24:54.260 --> 00:24:55.433
Hmm, I understand.

293
00:24:56.546 --> 00:24:57.296
Hmm.

294
00:24:57.976 --> 00:25:01.373
We need to take their statements. Hmm...

295
00:25:04.160 --> 00:25:05.626
That person from earlier is fine too.

296
00:25:06.260 --> 00:25:08.386
That's a relief.

297
00:25:10.443 --> 00:25:12.719
Wow, those bullies...

298
00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:15.403
High school students caught a gang member from the Yeonbaek Gang!

299
00:25:18.223 --> 00:25:20.339
Hey, why are you being like this?

300
00:25:20.340 --> 00:25:22.086
We didn't commit a crime.

301
00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:26.359
- The police station should give us a letter of appreciation. - Right...

302
00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:29.509
We didn't commit any crimes, and we were the ones who called the police.

303
00:25:29.510 --> 00:25:31.009
Stop talking, don't do this.

304
00:25:31.010 --> 00:25:32.020
Why?

305
00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:33.489
Who knows?

306
00:25:33.490 --> 00:25:35.810
This might even help us get into college!

307
00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:37.199
Really?

308
00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:39.270
Letter of appreciation my ass.

309
00:25:39.730 --> 00:25:41.819
Involving laws regarding the punishment of violent acts, etc.

310
00:25:41.820 --> 00:25:44.659
You should be thankful we didn't arrest you on the spot.

311
00:25:44.660 --> 00:25:45.183
What?

312
00:25:45.184 --> 00:25:48.329
You should have called the police immediately when you encountered the situation.

313
00:25:48.330 --> 00:25:49.939
Didn't you see the ambulance there?

314
00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:52.869
He was about to be beaten to death, how could we have time to call the police?

315
00:25:52.870 --> 00:25:55.379
Violence cannot be justified under any circumstances.

316
00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:56.206
That's the logic, right?

317
00:25:56.207 --> 00:25:58.679
Yeah, he's smart. He gets it.

318
00:25:58.680 --> 00:26:00.323
This mister is hilarious.

319
00:26:04.293 --> 00:26:08.710
However, that's only true when public authority is functioning properly.

320
00:26:10.540 --> 00:26:14.479
The public authority here is already terminally ill.

321
00:26:14.480 --> 00:26:15.353
Well...

322
00:26:16.896 --> 00:26:20.519
Although as a detective, I cannot praise you,

323
00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:24.906
